<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Line chart comparing five selection strategies by mean macro-F1 across three item budgets: eleven, nineteen, and twenty-six. All strategies improve with budget. Repeated random subsets and response-only adaptive selection show the highest mean macro-F1 at budget twenty-six, while fixed-order truncation consistently performs lowest.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing mean ECE-L across item budgets of eleven, nineteen, and twenty-six for response-only and RT calibration-only conditions, showing both metrics decrease as item budget increases, with RT calibration-only consistently lower.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing two methods: HCD-specific confidence only \(blue\) and HCD-specific confidence plus response time \(orange\), showing percentage of scale-level HCD decisions captured versus percentage of participants escalated, with the combined method consistently capturing more decisions at each escalation level.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
